    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7681" root="حرف" body-key="H">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">احرف</span></b> : see 1. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, (inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِحْرَافٌ</span>, Msb,)
<i>His</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مال</span> [or <i>cattle</i>] <i>increased, and became in a
good state</i> or <i>condition.</i> (AZ, S, Msb, K.) One
says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَآءَ بِالحَقِ وَالإِحْرَافِ</span>, meaning <i>He came
with,</i> or <i>brought, much cattle.</i> (AZ, S. [See
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِلْقٌ</span>.]) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <i>He emaciated,</i> or <i>rendered lean,</i> a
she-camel: so says As: others say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">احرث</span>. (S.)
[See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَرْفٌ</span>: and see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَرِيثَةٌ</span>.] ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  See also 3, last
sentence but one.

